{
  "characters": [
    {
      "name": "Ajax of Salamis — The Shield",
      "description": "Ajax is a **towering man of forty**, with deep brown eyes, weathered olive skin, a broken nose, and thick black curls threaded with grey. An old spear wound puckers his left shoulder. He wears practical bronze armour, heavy wool cloaks, and plain linen garments, all repaired rather than replaced. *Even at rest, he seems to stand between someone and danger.*",
      "backstory": "This version of **Ajax of Salamis** brought the surviving ships into the sheltered harbour after a disastrous campaign. He promised that every person aboard would reach home, including prisoners his officers would rather abandon.\n\nNow the harbour mouth opens each dawn onto an unfamiliar sea. Ajax believes the fleet must sail together or remain together, although dwindling provisions are making that promise dangerous. *What is strength worth if it cannot carry everyone?*"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ajax of Salamis — The Exile",
      "description": "Ajax is a **broad, powerful man of thirty-three**, with copper-brown skin, closely cropped dark hair, hazel eyes, and a narrow burn scar running from his jaw to his collarbone. His beard grows unevenly over an old cut. He favours sailors’ linen, worn leather belts, and unadorned travelling cloaks; the pale band on one finger marks a missing signet ring. *He watches doorways before faces.*",
      "backstory": "This version of **Ajax of Salamis** surrendered his command after refusing an order to burn an inhabited island. His own captains declared him a traitor, and he reached the harbour aboard a fishing boat.\n\nThe stranded fleet needs his knowledge of the western passages, but restoring his authority would also restore the men who condemned him. He wants a voyage toward a new home, free of inherited loyalties. *He has not decided whether that means leaving his people behind.*"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ajax of Salamis — The Listener",
      "description": "Ajax is a **massive man of fifty-two**, with sun-darkened skin, a square face, silver-streaked black braids, and a neatly trimmed grey beard. One eye is clouded; the other is a warm, attentive brown. His hands bear both sword calluses and small carving scars. He wears loose linen, woven shawls, and weathered bronze ornaments, carrying weapons without military finery. *His stillness invites confessions.*",
      "backstory": "This version of **Ajax of Salamis** survived a shipwreck by following a voice beneath the water. Since then, he has heard drowned sailors speaking through shells, bilges, and rain barrels.\n\nThey insist the harbour shelters something the fleet must return before any voyage can lead home. Ajax seeks the truth behind their demands, while fearing that obedience will cost living sailors their lives. *He remembers every dead voice more clearly than his own children's laughter.*"
    }
  ],
  "npcs": [
    {
      "name": "Ajax of Locris",
      "description": "Ajax is a **lean man of thirty-six**, with tawny skin, restless dark eyes, short black curls, and a pointed beard. A silver tooth flashes when he smiles, and rope burns circle both wrists. He favours light linen tunics, short travelling cloaks, and flexible leather armour. *He moves like a man expecting either applause or a knife.*",
      "backstory": "Known as **the other Ajax**, the Locrian captain arrived with the fastest ship and the fewest survivors. He claims the changing sea can be mastered by speed and nerve, and secretly possesses a chart that updates itself in seawater.\n\nHe stole that chart from a drowned shrine. Its newest markings resemble the streets of his childhood home.",
      "relationships": "He treats whichever version of Ajax of Salamis is chosen as an indispensable rival, alternating between genuine affection and bitter competition. **He wants the two Ajaxes to sail first**, even if the rest of the fleet must wait. Captain Thaleia distrusts his chart; Neris recognises the shrine depicted along its border."
    },
    {
      "name": "Thaleia Reed",
      "description": "Thaleia is a **stocky woman of forty-seven**, with dark brown skin, close-shaved hair, amber eyes, and a broad nose dusted with pale freckles. Two fingers are missing from her right hand. She wears durable sailors’ trousers, layered linen shirts, and sleeveless wool coats with generously sized pockets. *Her expression suggests she has already checked the knots herself.*",
      "backstory": "A former grain captain, Thaleia became harbourmaster after towing three warships through the sheltering reefs. She knows the fleet has less than a fortnight of food, despite the reassuring figures posted at the quay.\n\nShe is quietly converting a ceremonial barge into a vessel for children and wounded passengers. **She will launch it without permission if the commanders delay too long.**",
      "relationships": "Thaleia controls berths, stores, and departure crews, making her essential to every version of the protagonist. She employs Meles and protects his family. She respects Ajax of Salamis but challenges promises unsupported by provisions; she considers Ajax of Locris dangerously persuasive."
    },
    {
      "name": "Neris of the Lower Steps",
      "description": "Neris is a **slender woman of about sixty**, with pale brown skin, long white hair worn in loose plaits, and large grey eyes filmed by cataracts. Blue pigment stains her fingertips, and small shell beads hang from her ears. She typically wears layered undyed robes, knitted wraps, and soft leather shoes. *She tilts her head toward water as others turn toward speech.*",
      "backstory": "Neris once tended the shrine beneath the harbour cliffs. When an earthquake submerged it, she survived by clinging to its wooden door for three days.\n\nShe believes the shifting sea began when a sacred chart was removed, but returning it would require flooding the lower harbour, where refugees now live. **Her knowledge offers a remedy with a human cost.**",
      "relationships": "Neris approaches any chosen Ajax of Salamis with a request to investigate the submerged shrine. She suspects Ajax of Locris of theft and needs Meles to guide her through the flooded passages. Thaleia insists that no ritual proceed before the lower quay is evacuated."
    },
    {
      "name": "Meles",
      "description": "Meles is a **wiry young man of nineteen**, with brown skin, wide-set green eyes, tightly curled auburn hair, and a chipped front tooth. A childhood injury leaves him with a slight limp on land, though he swims easily. He wears patched fishermen’s clothes, woven reed hats, and practical cord necklaces used to secure small tools. *He smiles most freely below the notice of officers.*",
      "backstory": "Meles grew up diving for lost anchors and selling recovered nails. His family now shares a warehouse with displaced islanders, and he has begun charging desperate sailors for fragments of information about the reef channels.\n\nOn his latest dive, he found a ship beneath the harbour bearing fresh repairs he had watched Thaleia make only yesterday. **Its hold contained belongings from people who have not yet sailed.**",
      "relationships": "Meles becomes the protagonist’s guide to the harbour’s submerged places, whatever Ajax is chosen. Thaleia is his employer and reluctant guardian; Neris taught him the old shrine’s layout. Ajax of Locris offers enough money for his discoveries to buy his family passage, provided he tells nobody else."
    }
  ]
}
